{"type": "sena", "_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"content": "The Natural World", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": " Our Natural Environment", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 4, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 12, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "B1.2", "type": "level"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": "Exchange advice and suggestions in communicative situations.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations.", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations.", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations.", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations.", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations.", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations.", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations.", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations.", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Intonation in Long Questions", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "Intonation is important in long questions. You use the rise and fall of your voice to show the listener when you are or are not finished.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "In long questions, the intonation falls and then rises to show the question is not finished. The intonation rises or falls at the end, depending on whether it is an information or yes/no question.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Say these sentences. Vary the intonation on the bolded words. Be sure to notice if the question is an information or yes/no question.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Have you settled in <span class=\"strong\"> yet </span>or are you just getting to <span class=\"strong\"> know</span> the <span class=\"strong\"> place</span>? ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "What's more important to <span class=\"strong\">you</span>: hitting on your <span class=\"strong\"> neighbor</span> or saving the<span class=\"strong\"> narwhal</span>?", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to settle in", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to become comfortable in a new place ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Have you settled in yet?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le12ob04aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": " These are words you use to talk about nature.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "green", "type": "name"}, {"content": "environmentally friendly ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: My building is very \u2018green'.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le12ob04aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "recycling", "type": "name"}, {"content": "converting garbage into useful material ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: My building has strict recycling rules.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le12ob04aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "knack ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "an acquired or natural skill at performing a task", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I've got quite the knack for knowing what goes where.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le12ob04aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "narwhal", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a small Arctic whale, the male has a long forward-pointing spiralled tusk  ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I saw an article yesterday about a narwhal.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le12ob04aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "tree hugger ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a person who is very environmentally aware  ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: You're such a tree hugger.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le12ob04aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "chute", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a slide for moving things to a lower level ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Sometimes I put recyclable materials down the garbage chute.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le12ob04aud07", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": " Silent Letters in English ", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You don't say every letter in a word in English pronunciation.<br/><br/>Here there are examples of silent letters in words. Practice by saying the example sentences.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":9,\"columns\":3,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Letter\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Words\\\"}\